Log Core Restart Counter
    [Documentation]  Checks coreRestartCounter value for every detected system module. If coreRestartCounter value >
    ...              acceptable_number_of_resets, logs it with WARN level.
    [Arguments]      ${acceptable_number_of_resets}=0
    ...              ${bts_type}=GNB

    ${connection}     connections.get_default_admin_connection_alias    bts_type=${bts_type}
    ${smods}          admin.get_managed_objects   class_name=SMOD_L
    ...                                           connection=${connection}

    FOR   ${smod}    IN    @{smods}
        ${num_of_resets}    Set variable    ${smod['parameters']['coreRestartCounter']}
        ${sn}               Set variable    ${smod['parameters']['serialNumber']}
        Run Keyword If  ${num_of_resets == None}  Robot Log Step
        ...                                SMOD (sn: ${sn}): cannot get coreRestartCounter.
        ...    ELSE IF  ${num_of_resets} <= ${acceptable_number_of_resets}  Robot Log Step
        ...                                SMOD (sn: ${sn}): an allowed numer of kernel restarts.
        ...    ELSE     Robot Log Warning
        ...                                SMOD (sn: ${sn}): not allowed number (${num_of_resets}) of kernel restarts.
    END

